    <p>While color matters, rating differential is the single strongest predictor of game outcome. The correlation between (white_rating − black_rating) and white victory is <strong>r = 0.367</strong> — a moderate-to-strong effect in a domain with high variance. The higher-rated player wins 64.6% of decisive games, dwarfing the first-move advantage in predictive power.</p>

