    <p>The mean rating differential (white − black) is +7.8 points, with a median of +3.0 and a standard deviation of 249.0. The near-zero mean confirms random pairing; the large standard deviation reflects Lichess's open pool, where 2,900+ rating gaps are not uncommon.</p>

