    <p>The relationship between rating differential and win probability is strikingly linear. When white is 200+ points lower-rated, white wins just 21.7% of games. At near-parity (−50 to 0), the rate is exactly 50.0%. When white enjoys a 200+ point advantage, the win rate jumps to 81.8%. This pattern validates the Elo system's theoretical predictions and demonstrates that rating is a highly reliable outcome predictor on Lichess.</p>

